# Candidate report contract 0.1

Use this portable candidate file for the Skill's output. The TraceAudit engine
and six-module handoff have their own response formats. The rules are the ten
unchanged files from `audit/traceaudit-r12` in FormSyAI/formsy-sop commit
`8a57dcf33658844f6852fb144c3943ab4a3fed4d`. The release SHA-256 is
`f749e17f38821844b3c5322f3b295bae25c37f1011d91887e608a84c6202ef08`.
The digest identifies the frozen bytes. Verify the publisher and its claims
separately.

The nine entries in frozen `release.json` are seven rule sources, the
compiled catalog, and the README. The script checks the release file against
the fixed hash above. Retain `reference_only=true`,
`source_authenticated=false`, interpretation revision `1.9.1`, and machine
contract `1.9`. The compiled catalog contains 33 rules, 144 conditions, and
184 atomic obligations. Use `coverage_manifest` to distinguish retained source
text from compiled coverage. Upstream source-code provenance, relative links,
and engine commands are historical references.

Use the top-level fields in the candidate template.

| Field | Requirement |
| --- | --- |
| `schema_version` | `traceaudit-candidate-0.1` |
| `task_id`, `target_version`, `round_id` | Nonempty values for this round. Use a new round for reinterpretation or retest. |
| `rule_binding` | Match the frozen release, release and compiled SHA-256 values, interpretation revision, machine contract and digest, and both source flags. |
| `profile` | `code_fix` or `full_sop`, chosen before evaluation. Keep the chosen scope when a check fails. |
| `scope` | Use mode `selected_conditions` or `all_registered_conditions` and distinct `condition_ids`. The latter mode requires all 144. Omitted conditions remain unreviewed. |
| `triggers` | Use the three keys `design_full`, `formal_closure`, and `full_security`, each with `status`, `reason`, and `source_refs`. Use `triggered`, `not_requested`, or `uncertain`. The first two triggers require original user or assistant citations. Without a source, use `uncertain`. |
| `sources` | Each row contains `id/path/revision/task_id/target_version/role/sha256/read_extent`. Use a path relative to the report directory or an absolute local path. Record the source's own revision. Roles are user/assistant/source/test/commit_diff/context/runtime. Use one-based inclusive line coordinates for the actual extent read. The script checks bytes and quotes. Verify role and metadata authenticity independently. |
| `conditions` | Provide a row for every selected condition with `condition_id/status/reason/source_refs/items`. Include all registered items under each condition, with `item_id/status/reason/source_refs`. Use satisfied/unsatisfied/unverified/not_applicable. Cite evidence for determinate statuses and explain any unverified result. |
| `analysis_failures`, `known_limits` | Record unexecuted stages, truncation, extraction and citation failures, coverage gaps, and known upstream residuals. |
| `analysis_complete` | Use true only when all 144 conditions have complete rows and analysis has no failures. Keep unverified results and assess evidence sufficiency and semantic accuracy separately. |
| `capabilities` | Keep `source_identity_checked/runtime_identity_checked/execution_performed` false. Evaluate identity and execution separately from file hashes. |
| `formal_closed` | Keep false. Record actual closure, approval, and stage confirmation separately. |

Every `source_ref` includes
`source_id/revision/task_id/target_version/start_line/end_line/quote`. Match
the source metadata and report task, keep the coordinates inside
`read_extent`, and quote the exact text within that range. Source files can
be uploaded or manually prepared text. Treat their metadata binding as a
report claim. Require a trusted adapter for a trusted runtime conclusion.
Check source, role, coverage, and support for the finding separately from
the byte and quote checks.

Aggregate composite conditions using the original contract and retain
independent parent evidence gates. The model must separately record semantic
checks, role authenticity, TC14 coverage, interpretation of trigger scope,
root-cause reasoning, and the resulting gaps. Explanations such as
`semantic_basis` may be added to items. Follow the evidence contract for 1.9
before declaring a gate met. An entirely unverified report can still pass
structural validation.

Bind new reports explicitly to `interpretation_revision=1.9.1`. Keep r11
for retrospective review. Validate historical reports with their original
Skill version and rules and preserve their bindings and conclusions.
